From f7112d8f2e64644e69a9c174d44716575b19edab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:30:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: GitHub Actions runner never persisted data/ across daily
 runs

.gitignore excluded data/*.csv and data/*.json, so the daily_crawl.yml
workflow's 'git add data/ docs/ reports/' step silently added nothing
from data/ even though it clearly intended to (the workflow was
written assuming data/ would persist across runs).

Each Actions run starts from a fresh checkout with an empty data/
folder, so every day: get_previous_dataset() found no prior CSV (no
real rank_delta baseline), and export_static_web_dataset()'s date
listing (glob over data/ranking_*.csv) only ever saw *today's* just-
scraped CSV. That overwrote docs/dates.json down to a single entry
every run, breaking the date selector and freezing the visible
'latest' date at whatever day the bug's effect was last visible
(2026-09-26).

Fixes:
- Un-ignore data/*.csv and data/*.json so the workflow's existing
  'git add data/' actually persists history across runs going
  forward.
- Defense in depth: export_static_web_dataset() now also folds in
  any date already present as docs/data_<date>.json, so dates.json
  can never regress below what's already published even if data/
  is ever empty/incomplete again for some other reason.
- Immediately rebuilt docs/dates.json / docs/history_list.json from
  the 22 data_<date>.json files already sitting in docs/ (2026-08-27
  through 2026-09-26), so the date selector is fixed right away
  without waiting on the next scheduled run.

Separately: 2026-09-27 and 2026-09-28 have no crawl commits at all,
which this fix doesn't fully explain -- worth checking the Actions
tab run logs for those two days directly.
